  "answer": "No. A recorded supervision event or completed reconciliation may support an assessment, but neither alone establishes adequate supervision or proper ownership records. That conclusion requires an applicable substantive standard and reliable facts showing that the relevant actor met it across the relevant activity and period. The retained provisions supply qualitative requirements and considerations, not an event-count or reconciliation-completion safe harbour.",
